# Force-update floor for the beam desktop app. A client below this version is
# blocked out of the panel until it updates; empty means no floor, which is the
# normal case.
#
# Set it ONLY when an older build must not stay in use - a security fix in the
# app, or a wire change it cannot survive. Raising it locks every client below
# the value out until they update, so it is deliberately not an operator setting
# in the panel: it is a property of the release, and whoever cuts the release
# sets it here.
#
# The value is baked into the SIGNED release manifest by beam-release at tag
# time, so it takes effect with the NEXT release and stays in force until this
# file changes. Both readers verify the manifest signature before trusting it:
# Core (effectiveMinVersion) advertises it, the app (belowMinVersion) enforces it.
#
# Must be exactly x.y.z. beam-release refuses anything the app's own parser would
# silently ignore, because an unparseable floor is not a loud failure - it is a
# gate that quietly never fires.
MIN_VERSION=
